[SIZE="4"][B]RPQuest[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE="4"][COLOR="DarkRed"][B]Notice:[/B][/COLOR] I'm actively developing this. Being a social-focused addon there are many aspects that I need to test with others. If you are willing to help test it or have comments, contact me![/SIZE]

A native, [B]zero-dependency[/B] add-on for [B]The Elder Scrolls Online[/B] that lets you create, play, complete, and share [B]custom Roleplay quests[/B] directly inside ESO's native UI.

[SIZE="3"][B]Key Features[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Native Quest Journal Integration (J):[/B] Adds a dedicated [B]RPQuest[/B] tab inside the standard Quest Journal with separate [B]Prepared[/B] (authored) and [B]Received[/B] (active/playable) quest lists.
[*][B]Reticle NPC Target Capture:[/B] Aim at any living NPC and press your keybind to register objectives automatically. Capturing the same NPC name multiple times stacks into [I]Imp x3[/I]; different named NPCs are tracked individually, with optional per-target location conditions ([I]Required[/I] / [I]Not Required[/I]) and custom elimination messages.
[*][B]Hidden Discovery Points:[/B] Capture in-world exploration coordinates with configurable trigger radii ([I]Small[/I], [I]Medium[/I], [I]Large[/I]) without cluttering the map or compass with spoilers.
[*][B]Optional Stealth / Undetected Condition:[/B] Require players to complete objectives without being detected in combat.
[*][B]World Map Search Area (M):[/B] Displays an approximate search circle on the World Map using a deterministic, fixed random offset—keeping the target inside the circle without revealing its exact center. Automatically clears upon completion or deactivation.
[*][B]Native NPC Dialogue Injection:[/B] Bind custom RPQuest dialogue lines and per-NPC player response options to native ESO NPCs (via reticle capture or NPC name), injected seamlessly into the native interaction window without altering original NPC options.
[*][B]Combat & Discovery Tracking + Native Alerts:[/B] Tracks kills and exploration proximity, triggering native Center Screen Announcements and official quest sounds.
[*][B]HUD Mini-Tracker:[/B] Displays the active custom quest on the side of your screen (left-click opens the Journal; right-click centers the World Map on the search area).
[*][B]1-to-1 In-Game Mail Flow (No Copy/Paste):[/B] Assign a single [I]@AccountName[/I] recipient directly in the quest editor and send the quest with one click (automatically splitting larger quests up to 6 parts via [I]RPQP[/I] on the same megaserver). Incoming quest mails are automatically ingested into the player's [B]Pending[/B] list with an alert and [B]Accept[/B] / [B]Reject[/B] buttons. Completing or rejecting a quest automatically mails the result back to the Quest Master, updating the prepared quest status ([I]Draft[/I] / [I]Sent[/I] / [I]Completed[/I] / [I]Rejected[/I]).
[*][B]Per-Character Persistence & Auto-Localization:[/B] Stores progress per character via SavedVariables and auto-detects client language (English / Spanish).
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Keybinds (Settings -> Controls -> RPQuest)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Capture Target under Reticle:[/B] Captures the living NPC currently under your reticle into the quest draft.
[*][B]Capture Discovery Point:[/B] Captures your current character position as a hidden discovery objective.
[*][B]Toggle Custom Quests Tab:[/B] Opens or closes the Quest Journal directly on the [B]RPQuest[/B] tab.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Quick Start[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*][B]Create a Quest:[/B] Open the Quest Journal ([B]J[/B]), switch to the [B]RPQuest[/B] tab, and click [B]Create Quest[/B]. Use the collapsible sections to set Title, Description, Search Area size, optional Stealth condition, and optional NPC Dialogue lines. Aim at NPCs or stand at discovery spots and press your keybinds.
[*][B]Send to a Player:[/B] Set the recipient [I]@AccountName[/I] in the quest editor and click [B]Send Quest[/B]. The player receives an alert and can [B]Accept[/B] or [B]Reject[/B] the quest directly from the [B]Pending[/B] section in their [B]RPQuest[/B] tab. Note: quests require the same game client language as the creator so NPC objectives and dialogues match.
[*][B]Play & Auto-Report:[/B] Accepting the quest activates the HUD mini-tracker, World Map search area, and injected NPC dialogues immediately. Upon completion or rejection, the result is automatically mailed back to the Quest Master.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="3"][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]External Libraries:[/B] None (Zero-Dependency)
[*][B]Languages:[/B] English (en), Spanish (es)
[/LIST]

